$NetBSD: patch-rts_rts.cabal,v 1.2 2026/11/13 14:26:06 pho Exp $

1. Fix build on macOS 26 (Tahoe). It has got a new implementation of ld
   which dislikes a hack used in rts. The upstream has a proper fix for
   this, but it's not included in 9.10 releases. -Wl,-ld_classic is just a
   short-term workaround and isn't going to be future-proof.
   https://gitlab.haskell.org/ghc/ghc/-/work_items/26166

2. Fix build on Illumos where ld(1) dislikes undefined symbols in
   executables just like MacOS X.
   https://gitlab.haskell.org/ghc/ghc/-/merge_requests/12613

--- rts/rts.cabal.orig	2025-09-10 16:02:37.000000000 +0000
+++ rts/rts.cabal
@@ -331,9 +331,15 @@ library
                     "-Wl,-U,___darwin_check_fd_set_overflow"
                     -- See Note [Undefined symbols in the RTS]
                     "-Wl,-undefined,dynamic_lookup"
+        if arch(aarch64)
+           ld-options: -Wl,-ld_classic
         if !arch(x86_64) && !arch(aarch64)
            ld-options: -read_only_relocs warning
 
+      if os(solaris2)
+        ld-options: "-Wl,-z,nodefs"
+        -- See Note [Undefined symbols in the RTS]
+
       cmm-sources: Apply.cmm
                    Compact.cmm
                    ContinuationOps.cmm
